#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-am(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:7
msgid "git-am - Apply a series of patches from a mailbox"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'git am' [--signoff] [--keep] [--[no-]keep-cr] [--[no-]utf8] [--no-verify]\n"
"\t [--[no-]3way] [--interactive] [--committer-date-is-author-date]\n"
"\t [--ignore-date] [--ignore-space-change | --ignore-whitespace]\n"
"\t [--whitespace=<action>] [-C<n>] [-p<n>] [--directory=<dir>]\n"
"\t [--exclude=<path>] [--include=<path>] [--reject] [-q | --quiet]\n"
"\t [--[no-]scissors] [-S[<keyid>]] [--patch-format=<format>]\n"
"\t [--quoted-cr=<action>]\n"
"\t [--empty=(stop|drop|keep)]\n"
"\t [(<mbox> | <Maildir>)...]\n"
"'git am' (--continue | --skip | --abort | --quit | --retry | "
"--show-current-patch[=(diff|raw)] | --allow-empty)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:30
msgid ""
"Splits mail messages in a mailbox into commit log messages, authorship "
"information, and patches, and applies them to the current branch. You could "
"think of it as a reverse operation of linkgit:git-format-patch[1] run on a "
"branch with a straight history without merges."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "(<mbox>|<Maildir>)..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:37
msgid ""
"The list of mailbox files to read patches from. If you do not supply this "
"argument, the command reads from the standard input.  If you supply "
"directories, they will be treated as Maildirs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-s::`\n"
"`--signoff::`\n"
"\tAdd a `Signed-off-by` trailer to the commit message, using\n"
"\tthe committer identity of yourself.\n"
"\tSee the signoff option in linkgit:git-commit[1] for more information.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-k::`\n"
"`--keep::`\n"
"\tPass `-k` flag to 'git mailinfo' (see linkgit:git-mailinfo[1]).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--keep-non-patch::`\n"
"\tPass `-b` flag to 'git mailinfo' (see linkgit:git-mailinfo[1]).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]keep-cr::`\n"
"\tWith `--keep-cr`, call 'git mailsplit' (see linkgit:git-mailsplit[1])\n"
"\twith the same option, to prevent it from stripping CR at the end of\n"
"\tlines. `am.keepcr` configuration variable can be used to specify the\n"
"\tdefault behaviour.  `--no-keep-cr` is useful to override `am.keepcr`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-c::`\n"
"`--scissors::`\n"
"\tRemove everything in body before a scissors line (see\n"
"\tlinkgit:git-mailinfo[1]). Can be activated by default using\n"
"\tthe `mailinfo.scissors` configuration variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--no-scissors::`\n"
"\tIgnore scissors lines (see linkgit:git-mailinfo[1]).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--quoted-cr=<action>::`\n"
"\tThis flag will be passed down to 'git mailinfo' (see "
"linkgit:git-mailinfo[1]).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:71
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--empty=(drop|keep|stop)::`\n"
"\tHow to handle an e-mail message lacking a patch:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "`drop`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:75
msgid "The e-mail message will be skipped."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:75
#, no-wrap
msgid "`keep`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:78
msgid ""
"An empty commit will be created, with the contents of the e-mail message as "
"its log."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "`stop`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:81
msgid ""
"The command will fail, stopping in the middle of the current `am` "
"session. This is the default behavior."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-m::`\n"
"`--message-id::`\n"
"\tPass the `-m` flag to 'git mailinfo' (see linkgit:git-mailinfo[1]),\n"
"\tso that the Message-ID header is added to the commit message.\n"
"\tThe `am.messageid` configuration variable can be used to specify\n"
"\tthe default behaviour.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--no-message-id::`\n"
"\tDo not add the Message-ID header to the commit message.\n"
"\t`no-message-id` is useful to override `am.messageid`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:97
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-q::`\n"
"`--quiet::`\n"
"\tBe quiet. Only print error messages.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-u::`\n"
"`--utf8::`\n"
"\tPass `-u` flag to 'git mailinfo' (see linkgit:git-mailinfo[1]).\n"
"\tThe proposed commit log message taken from the e-mail\n"
"\tis re-coded into UTF-8 encoding (configuration variable\n"
"\t`i18n.commitEncoding` can be used to specify the project's\n"
"\tpreferred encoding if it is not UTF-8).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:108
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This was optional in prior versions of git, but now it is the\n"
"default.   You can use `--no-utf8` to override this.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:112
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--no-utf8::`\n"
"\tPass `-n` flag to 'git mailinfo' (see\n"
"\tlinkgit:git-mailinfo[1]).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:122
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-3::`\n"
"`--3way::`\n"
"`--no-3way::`\n"
"\tWhen the patch does not apply cleanly, fall back on\n"
"\t3-way merge if the patch records the identity of blobs\n"
"\tit is supposed to apply to and we have those blobs\n"
"\tavailable locally. `--no-3way` can be used to override\n"
"\tam.threeWay configuration variable. For more information,\n"
"\tsee am.threeWay in linkgit:git-config[1].\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:137
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--ignore-space-change::`\n"
"`--ignore-whitespace::`\n"
"`--whitespace=<action>::`\n"
"`-C<n>::`\n"
"`-p<n>::`\n"
"`--directory=<dir>::`\n"
"`--exclude=<path>::`\n"
"`--include=<path>::`\n"
"`--reject::`\n"
"\tThese flags are passed to the 'git apply' (see linkgit:git-apply[1])\n"
"\tprogram that applies\n"
"\tthe patch.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:140
msgid ""
"Valid <action> for the `--whitespace` option are: `nowarn`, `warn`, `fix`, "
"`error`, and `error-all`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--patch-format::`\n"
"\tBy default the command will try to detect the patch format\n"
"\tautomatically. This option allows the user to bypass the automatic\n"
"\tdetection and specify the patch format that the patch(es) should be\n"
"\tinterpreted as. Valid formats are mbox, mboxrd,\n"
"\tstgit, stgit-series, and hg.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:151
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-i::`\n"
"`--interactive::`\n"
"\tRun interactively.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:157
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-n::`\n"
"`--no-verify::`\n"
"\tBy default, the pre-applypatch and applypatch-msg hooks are run.\n"
"\tWhen any of `--no-verify` or `-n` is given, these are bypassed.\n"
"\tSee also linkgit:githooks[5].\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:164
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--committer-date-is-author-date::`\n"
"\tBy default the command records the date from the e-mail\n"
"\tmessage as the commit author date, and uses the time of\n"
"\tcommit creation as the committer date. This allows the\n"
"\tuser to lie about the committer date by using the same\n"
"\tvalue as the author date.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:171
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--ignore-date::`\n"
"\tBy default the command records the date from the e-mail\n"
"\tmessage as the commit author date, and uses the time of\n"
"\tcommit creation as the committer date. This allows the\n"
"\tuser to lie about the author date by using the same\n"
"\tvalue as the committer date.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:175
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--skip::`\n"
"\tSkip the current patch.  This is only meaningful when\n"
"\trestarting an aborted patch.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:184
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-S[<keyid>]::`\n"
"`--gpg-sign[=<keyid>]::`\n"
"`--no-gpg-sign::`\n"
"\tGPG-sign commits. The `keyid` argument is optional and\n"
"\tdefaults to the committer identity; if specified, it must be\n"
"\tstuck to the option without a space. `--no-gpg-sign` is useful to\n"
"\tcountermand both `commit.gpgSign` configuration variable, and\n"
"\tearlier `--gpg-sign`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:194
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--continue::`\n"
"`-r::`\n"
"`--resolved::`\n"
"\tAfter a patch failure (e.g. attempting to apply\n"
"\tconflicting patch), the user has applied it by hand and\n"
"\tthe index file stores the result of the application.\n"
"\tMake a commit using the authorship and commit log\n"
"\textracted from the e-mail message and the current index\n"
"\tfile, and continue.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:201
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--resolvemsg=<msg>::`\n"
"\tWhen a patch failure occurs, <msg> will be printed\n"
"\tto the screen before exiting.  This overrides the\n"
"\tstandard message informing you to use `--continue`\n"
"\tor `--skip` to handle the failure.  This is solely\n"
"\tfor internal use between 'git rebase' and 'git am'.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:206
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--abort::`\n"
"\tRestore the original branch and abort the patching operation.\n"
"\tRevert the contents of files involved in the am operation to their\n"
"\tpre-am state.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:210
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--quit::`\n"
"\tAbort the patching operation but keep HEAD and the index\n"
"\tuntouched.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:216
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--retry::`\n"
"\tTry to apply the last conflicting patch again. This is generally\n"
"\tonly useful for passing extra options to the retry attempt\n"
"\t(e.g., `--3way`), since otherwise you'll just see the same\n"
"\tfailure again.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:222
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--show-current-patch[=(diff|raw)]::`\n"
"\tShow the message at which `git am` has stopped due to\n"
"\tconflicts.  If `raw` is specified, show the raw contents of\n"
"\tthe e-mail message; if `diff`, show the diff portion only.\n"
"\tDefaults to `raw`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:227
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--allow-empty::`\n"
"\tAfter a patch failure on an input e-mail message lacking a patch,\n"
"\tcreate an empty commit with the contents of the e-mail message\n"
"\tas its log message.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:229
#, no-wrap
msgid "DISCUSSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:237
msgid ""
"The commit author name is taken from the \"From: \" line of the message, and "
"commit author date is taken from the \"Date: \" line of the message.  The "
"\"Subject: \" line is used as the title of the commit, after stripping "
"common prefix \"[PATCH <anything>]\".  The \"Subject: \" line is supposed to "
"concisely describe what the commit is about in one line of text."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:240
msgid ""
"\"From: \", \"Date: \", and \"Subject: \" lines starting the body override "
"the respective commit author name and title values taken from the headers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:245
msgid ""
"The commit message is formed by the title taken from the \"Subject: \", a "
"blank line and the body of the message up to where the patch begins.  Excess "
"whitespace at the end of each line is automatically stripped."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:248
msgid ""
"The patch is expected to be inline, directly following the message.  Any "
"line that is of the form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:250
msgid "three-dashes and end-of-line, or"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:251
msgid "a line that begins with \"diff -\", or"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:252
msgid "a line that begins with \"Index: \""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:255
msgid ""
"is taken as the beginning of a patch, and the commit log message is "
"terminated before the first occurrence of such a line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:259
msgid ""
"When initially invoking `git am`, you give it the names of the mailboxes to "
"process.  Upon seeing the first patch that does not apply, it aborts in the "
"middle.  You can recover from this in one of two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:262
msgid "skip the current patch by re-running the command with the `--skip` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:266
msgid ""
"hand resolve the conflict in the working directory, and update the index "
"file to bring it into a state that the patch should have produced.  Then run "
"the command with the `--continue` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:271
msgid ""
"The command refuses to process new mailboxes until the current operation is "
"finished, so if you decide to start over from scratch, run `git am --abort` "
"before running the command with mailbox names."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:277
msgid ""
"Before any patches are applied, ORIG_HEAD is set to the tip of the current "
"branch.  This is useful if you have problems with multiple commits, like "
"running 'git am' on the wrong branch or an error in the commits that is more "
"easily fixed by changing the mailbox (e.g.  errors in the \"From:\" lines)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:279
#, no-wrap
msgid "HOOKS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:283
msgid ""
"This command can run `applypatch-msg`, `pre-applypatch`, and "
"`post-applypatch` hooks.  See linkgit:githooks[5] for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-am.txt:285
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

